WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:00.990
- Welcome back, y'all.

00:00:00.990 --> 00:00:02.330
I'm here with Mike Colter,

00:00:02.330 --> 00:00:04.630
and on the line from
New York is Hoda Kotb.

00:00:04.630 --> 00:00:06.373
Give it up for 'em!

00:00:06.373 --> 00:00:07.206
(audience applauds)

00:00:07.206 --> 00:00:10.470
All right, so, in this
time of global pandemic,

00:00:10.470 --> 00:00:11.998
we're always on the phone.

00:00:11.998 --> 00:00:14.460
We are also not allowed to touch anything

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:15.680
another human touches,

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:17.990
which means, no games that
involve hitting a button

00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:18.823
on a podium.

00:00:18.823 --> 00:00:22.887
So, fear not, though, people,
in honor of Hoda's new book,

00:00:22.887 --> 00:00:24.090
"This Just Speaks to Me,"

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:27.230
we have a solution in the
form of the game called

00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:28.660
Hoda the phone.

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:31.576
(phone rings)

00:00:31.576 --> 00:00:33.147
♪ Hoda the phone ♪

00:00:33.147 --> 00:00:36.594
- Hoda the phone. We're awesome.

00:00:36.594 --> 00:00:39.810
It's thick with the dad jokes today, Hoda.

00:00:39.810 --> 00:00:41.820
Okay. Here's how it works.

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:44.380
Mike Colter and I each have a phone.

00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:46.256
Hoda will ask questions that have to do

00:00:46.256 --> 00:00:49.200
with scary movies in honor of Halloween

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:51.300
and Mike's new show "Monster Land."

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:55.076
After Hoda asks the question,
we will hear the sound.

00:00:55.076 --> 00:00:56.650
(phone rings)

00:00:56.650 --> 00:00:58.600
Whoever grabs their phone first,

00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:01.640
and gives the correct
answer, gets the point.

00:01:01.640 --> 00:01:04.580
If you're wrong, the
other person can steal.

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:09.300
Most points wins, but Hoda
the phone, there's a twist.

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:12.720
If you touch the phone before it rings,

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:14.150
you're disqualified from the question.

00:01:14.150 --> 00:01:15.750
I'm pretty sure that my
producers put that in

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:18.360
just to screw me. Pretty sure.

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:20.890
I'll play it for the right
side of the audience.

00:01:20.890 --> 00:01:22.850
Mike is playing for the left.

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:26.920
The winner gets a $200 gift
card to OtterBox for their side.

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:27.753
You're welcome.

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:30.390
Okay, so Hoda, let's go.

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:31.693
What's the first question, ma'am?

00:01:31.693 --> 00:01:33.257
- All right. All right, here we go.

00:01:33.257 --> 00:01:35.540
In "Carrie" -

00:01:35.540 --> 00:01:36.373
- [Kelly] Uh oh.

00:01:36.373 --> 00:01:40.008
- What did the other students
dump on Carrie at the prom?

00:01:40.008 --> 00:01:43.060
(phone rings)

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:43.948
- Am I talking to you?

00:01:43.948 --> 00:01:44.900
What am I doing?

00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:46.080
I'm going to say it out loud?

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:47.175
Pig's blood.

00:01:47.175 --> 00:01:48.293
- What?

00:01:48.293 --> 00:01:49.420
- Yes.

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:50.253
- Oh my gosh.

00:01:50.253 --> 00:01:51.086
I've never seen that movie.

00:01:51.086 --> 00:01:53.340
No, no, nope.

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:55.010
- Okay. Kelly, you talk smack.

00:01:55.010 --> 00:01:56.160
Let's go, babe. Get in it.

00:01:56.160 --> 00:01:57.543
- [Kelly] I don't do scary.

00:01:57.543 --> 00:02:01.450
- The title of this scary movie
is also what you might say

00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:04.469
to someone whom you want to leave.

00:02:04.469 --> 00:02:05.720
(phone rings)

00:02:05.720 --> 00:02:07.150
- Who you want to leave?

00:02:07.150 --> 00:02:10.863
Bye. Bye.

00:02:12.237 --> 00:02:14.717
"Bye, Bye, Birdie."

00:02:16.020 --> 00:02:17.570
Get out of here. Get out!

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:19.073
Oh! "Get Out!"

00:02:19.073 --> 00:02:19.906
- Duh!

00:02:20.855 --> 00:02:23.427
- Oh, my God. I said "Bye, Bye, Birdie."

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:26.130
- God, I was like, I was struggling.

00:02:26.130 --> 00:02:27.376
I was following, you.

00:02:27.376 --> 00:02:28.959
I was like, bye, bye, what?

00:02:28.959 --> 00:02:30.740
- Okay, one, one, kiddos.

00:02:30.740 --> 00:02:31.820
One, one, here we go.

00:02:31.820 --> 00:02:32.653
- God.

00:02:32.653 --> 00:02:36.000
- What scary movie is
based on a real life doll

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:37.770
that lived in Key West, Florida,

00:02:37.770 --> 00:02:41.980
and was allegedly placed
under a voodoo curse?

00:02:41.980 --> 00:02:43.870
- Is that, wait, is that -

00:02:43.870 --> 00:02:44.990
- Oh!

00:02:44.990 --> 00:02:45.823
- No!

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:47.770
- So, that doesn't count.

00:02:47.770 --> 00:02:49.523
So I win by default, right?

00:02:49.523 --> 00:02:50.790
- That is so wrong.

00:02:50.790 --> 00:02:53.280
- Right? She picked it up early.

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:54.484
- I think so.

00:02:54.484 --> 00:02:55.317
(phone rings)

00:02:55.317 --> 00:02:56.150
- Okay. I'll take a shot.

00:02:56.150 --> 00:02:57.190
A real live doll.

00:02:57.190 --> 00:02:58.023
- I mean there's only one, right?

00:02:58.023 --> 00:02:59.447
- It's "Chucky," right?

00:02:59.447 --> 00:03:00.490
"Chucky?" No?

00:03:01.810 --> 00:03:03.390
- No, dude, sorry.

00:03:03.390 --> 00:03:04.223
- It's not "Chucky"?

00:03:04.223 --> 00:03:05.547
- "Child's Play."

00:03:06.670 --> 00:03:09.470
- That's the doll's name,
though, Chucky, "Child's Play."

00:03:09.470 --> 00:03:10.856
- I think that kinda counts.

00:03:10.856 --> 00:03:12.290
I think that kinda counts.

00:03:12.290 --> 00:03:13.123
- [Mike] That counts.

00:03:13.123 --> 00:03:14.264
- [Hoda] Yeah, you get
it. You get it, Mike.

00:03:14.264 --> 00:03:15.097
- Yeah, gimme that, gimme that.

00:03:15.097 --> 00:03:16.470
- Okay, here we go. All right.

00:03:16.470 --> 00:03:19.143
So, it looks like the scales are tilted.

00:03:19.143 --> 00:03:20.411
- Well, ring the bell.

00:03:20.411 --> 00:03:21.290
Don't wait five hours.

00:03:21.290 --> 00:03:22.760
- No, give it three seconds.

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:24.274
- Here we go.

00:03:24.274 --> 00:03:27.240
What does Jack Nicholson
say when he finally

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:30.205
breaks through the door
with an ax in "The Shining"?

00:03:30.205 --> 00:03:31.910
(phone rings)

00:03:31.910 --> 00:03:33.853
- Here's Johnny.

00:03:34.772 --> 00:03:38.090
- You know what I was thinking,
actually, it was Redrum,

00:03:38.090 --> 00:03:39.905
but that's the kid, Redrum.

00:03:39.905 --> 00:03:40.738
It's murder.

00:03:40.738 --> 00:03:41.630
I actually didn't remember that.

00:03:41.630 --> 00:03:42.640
- All right, you sit and watch me play.

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:43.517
- I gotta be honest with you.

00:03:43.517 --> 00:03:44.568
I ain't never seen that either.

00:03:44.568 --> 00:03:45.520
- Sit and watch me play. I got this.

00:03:45.520 --> 00:03:46.353
- [Kelly] I'm out.

00:03:46.353 --> 00:03:47.186
- I love this game.

00:03:47.186 --> 00:03:49.000
- Okay, here we go.

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:50.750
Kelly, this one's triple or nothing.

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:51.880
So, you can actually win.

00:03:51.880 --> 00:03:53.839
- Okay, thank you. Thanks, Hoda.

00:03:53.839 --> 00:03:54.672
- [Mike] Okay.

00:03:54.672 --> 00:03:55.505
- You're welcome.

00:03:55.505 --> 00:03:57.940
A former cast member of "The Office"

00:03:57.940 --> 00:04:01.250
went on to direct the scary
movie called "A Quiet Place."

00:04:01.250 --> 00:04:02.430
Here's the question.

00:04:02.430 --> 00:04:04.947
What was his character's
name in "The Office?"

00:04:06.460 --> 00:04:09.210
- God, that, I should know this.

00:04:09.210 --> 00:04:10.973
A friend of mine is going
to kill me for this one.

00:04:10.973 --> 00:04:13.817
(phone rings)

00:04:13.817 --> 00:04:15.069
- I'm... John?

00:04:15.069 --> 00:04:16.257
- [Kelly] Jim?

00:04:16.257 --> 00:04:17.090
(buzzer rings)

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:17.923
- [Hoda] Jim.

00:04:17.923 --> 00:04:19.423
- Jim! Was it Jim?

00:04:20.263 --> 00:04:22.566
I thought it was Jim,
but I was too afraid.

00:04:22.566 --> 00:04:25.891
Oh my gosh, triple or nothing, sucker!

00:04:25.891 --> 00:04:26.998
- I should have known that one.

00:04:26.998 --> 00:04:30.192
- Obviously, Mike just killed me at that.

00:04:30.192 --> 00:04:31.025
- [Mike] I did.

00:04:31.025 --> 00:04:32.940
- But because this is the
Kelly Clarkson show, y'all,

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:34.820
everyone in our house seats is getting

00:04:34.820 --> 00:04:37.797
a $200 gift card for OtterBox.

00:04:37.797 --> 00:04:39.960
It's not only the number
one most trusted brand

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:41.440
for smartphone protection,

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:44.060
they have cases for
Apple watches, AirPods,

00:04:44.060 --> 00:04:45.900
screen protectors and more.

00:04:45.900 --> 00:04:47.210
Thank you so much, Hoda.

00:04:47.210 --> 00:04:48.490
It's so lovely to see you.

00:04:48.490 --> 00:04:50.072
- Love you, Kelly. Bye, Mike.

00:04:50.072 --> 00:04:50.933
- Bye!

